.TH WIVRN-LAYER-FILTER 7 "2026-10-20" "WiVRn Pro" "Miscellaneous Information"
.SH NAME
wivrn-layer-filter \- bounded minification filtering for desktop composition layers
.SH DESCRIPTION
WiVRn Pro can filter minified quad and cylinder textures using a locally estimated
output-pixel footprint. This reduces spatial aliasing in small or oblique desktop
windows without applying a full-frame blur. Gaze-driven encoding is independent.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B WIVRN_LAYER_FILTER=off
Default. Preserve the original bilinear sampling path.
.TP
.B WIVRN_LAYER_FILTER=balanced
Use up to two samples per footprint axis (four bilinear samples per pixel).
.TP
.B WIVRN_LAYER_FILTER=quality
Use up to four samples per footprint axis (sixteen bilinear samples per pixel).
.PP
Unknown values select off. Set the variable on wivrn-pro-server before startup,
not on DomeD or another OpenXR client. Restarting the server interrupts the stream.
.SH BEHAVIOR
Sampling ramps in between 1 and 1.5 times minification. Magnified textures retain
the original pixels. Taps are clamped to the submitted subimage, including flipped
coordinates and stereo halves. Projection layers and layers requesting
unpremultiplied or inverted alpha retain their original sampling path.
.SH PERFORMANCE
Footprint estimation adds GPU work even for magnified layers. The sample limit
bounds work but cannot exactly integrate arbitrarily large footprints. This is
not a mipmap implementation. Profile the actual headset workload before enabling.
.PP
The source distribution includes fork/tests/layer_filter_smoke.py. It compares
production shaders with float-buffer readback, excluding transfers from GPU
shader timings. Its synthetic timings are not headset latency or frame timings.
